  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LANDSCAPE APPROACH TO SAFEGUARD THE FUTURE OF BORNEAN ELEPHANT IN LOWER KINABATANGAN, SABAH, BORNEO, MALAYSIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO ENSURE THE LONG-TERM SURVIVAL OF WILD ASIAN ELEPHANTS IN KINABATANGAN, MALAYSIAN BORNEO THROUGH IMPLEMENTATION OF THE RECOMMENDATIONS IN THE NEW BORNEAN ELEPHANT ACTION PLAN 2020-2029 (BEAP 2020-2029) AND TO CONTINUE BUILDING THE CAPACITY OF YOUNG NATIONAL CONSERVATION PROFESSIONALS. THE ACTIVITIES PROPOSED WILL SUPPORT THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THREE MAJOR OBJECTIVES OF THE BEAP 2020-2029: (1) IMPROVE PROTECTION AND REDUCE ELEPHANT DEATHS (2) IMPROVE LANDSCAPE CONNECTIVITY AND PERMEABILITY AND (3) MONITOR AND PREDICT ELEPHANT POPULATION TRENDS. THIS WORK, TO BE IMPLEMENTED AT THE LANDSCAPE-LEVEL, IS SUPPORTED BY THE KINABATANGAN-BEAP TASKFORCE, LED BY THE KINABATANGAN DISTRICT OFFICE AND THE LOCAL GOVERNMENT, WHICH COORDINATE ALL DISTRICT LEVEL DEVELOPMENT ACTIVITIES. PROJECT ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) IMPROVE THE EFFICIENCY OF THE HONORARY WILDLIFE WARDEN NETWORK (2) UNDERTAKE REGULAR PATROLLING TO MONITOR ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES (3) DEVELOP AND SUPPORT EIGHT LOCAL RESIDENTS TO SERVE AS COMMUNITY ELEPHANT RANGER TEAMS IN TWO VILLAGES (4) TRAIN LOCAL COMMUNITIES AND OIL PALM PLANTATION WORKERS ON ELEPHANT BEHAVIOR (5) INVESTIGATE THE FEASIBILITY OF A PRIVATE INSURANCE PROGRAM (6) PRODUCE A 5- MINUTE VIRTUAL REALITY 360 VIDEO ABOUT HUMAN-ELEPHANT COEXISTENCE (7) PRECISE MAPPING AND CON</narrative>
  </description>
